Story: Seeing a friend who flies near you
  As a pilot with a TX15
  I want to see where the other pilots' planes are
  So that I keep clear of them

  A friend flies a plane near yours. At first the station only hears the Remote ID of the
  plane. Your friend joins the MAVLink network, and the station joins the two sources into
  one marker. Your friend lands and switches off, and the marker goes dim.

  Scenario: A friend joins and leaves
    When the other plane is sending Remote ID
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the map has 1 other plane
    And the source of the marker is Remote ID
    When the other plane is sending both
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the map has 1 other plane
    And the source of the marker is Remote ID and MAVLink
    When the other plane is silent
    And 10 seconds pass
    Then the marker of the other plane is stale
    When 70 seconds pass
    Then the map has 0 other planes

Story: Flying near a crowd of planes
  As a pilot with a TX15
  I want to see the planes that are in range, and no more
  So that I trust the map, and my telemetry stays good

  Planes that are too far away do not show. When a plane comes in range of the MAVLink
  network, it gets a marker. Then a crowd of pilots joins the network. The radio link is
  narrow, so the planes of the crowd cannot use all of it. Your own telemetry comes first.

  Scenario: Out of range, into range, into a crowd
    When the other plane is sending Remote ID
    And the distance to the other plane is 2000 m
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the map has 0 other planes
    When the other plane is sending MAVLink
    And the distance to the other plane is 7000 m
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the map has 0 other planes
    When the distance to the other plane is 1500 m
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the map has 1 other plane
    And the source of the marker is MAVLink
    When the crowd has 30 planes
    And 10 seconds pass
    Then the telemetry of your plane has at least 4 position updates per second

Story: Losing the radio link
  As a pilot with a TX15
  I want the map to tell me when it can no longer be right
  So that I do not trust old positions

  A friend flies near you, and the station tracks the plane. Then the radio link is lost. The
  station keeps the last position of the plane, and it dims the marker.

  Scenario: The link drops
    When the other plane is sending MAVLink
    And 5 seconds pass
    Then the marker of the other plane is live
    When the TX15 link is lost
    And 10 seconds pass
    Then the marker of the other plane is stale
